     155.2px at 30px against 246px of usable width (340 nav − 32 header
     padding − 16 brand padding − 36 mark − 10 gap), so 30px fits with 91px to
     spare. It is a proportion problem: at 30px the word runs 4.3× the mark's
     own width and the symbol reads as a bullet in front of a headline. The
     mark cannot meet it halfway — 36px is its floor, below which the gold
     star and the cutouts close into a blob — so the type is the only side
     with room to give. At 24px the word measures 124.2px, 3.5× the mark, and
     the pair reads as a mark with a name rather than a name with a mark. */
  .brand__product {
